# Digital Audio Synth

A small embedded firmware project for an STM32F446RE-based digital audio synthesizer and graphics demo. The repository contains a Cortex-M4 firmware build for driving an LCD, generating waveform data, and blinking a status LED using the STM32 hardware abstraction layer and CMSIS device headers.

## Overview

This project is designed around the STM32F446RE microcontroller and demonstrates:

- initializing the MCU clock and GPIO peripherals
- configuring SPI and LCD output
- drawing graphics primitives and waveforms on a connected LCD
- toggling the onboard user LED as a simple runtime heartbeat
- building firmware with a GNU ARM toolchain and flashing via ST-Link

The firmware is organized as a simple embedded application with custom LCD and utility modules plus vendor CMSIS and device support files for the STM32F446.

## Features

- STM32F446RE target support
- Cortex-M4 firmware build using `arm-none-eabi-gcc`
- SPI-based LCD initialization and updates
- Frame-buffer based drawing
- Waveform rendering including sine-wave output
- Simple LED heartbeat loop
- UART2 initialization helpers for serial output
- Makefile-based build and flash workflow

## Hardware

This project targets hardware compatible with the STM32F446RE MCU, including:

- STM32F446RE or similar Nucleo/Discovery-style board
- LCD display connected over SPI
- User LED on GPIOA pin 5 (configured in firmware)
- ST-Link programmer/debugger for flashing

## Repository Structure

```text
Digital-Audio-Synth/
├── Makefile                     # Build and flash rules
├── STM32F446RETX_FLASH.ld       # Linker script for flash memory layout
├── build/                       # Generated build artifacts
├── drivers/
│   ├── CMSIS/                   # CMSIS headers and DSP components
│   └── Device/                  # STM32F446 startup and device definitions
├── include/
│   ├── lcd.h                    # LCD driver API
│   └── util.h                   # Utility declarations
├── src/
│   ├── lcd.c                    # LCD driver implementation
│   ├── main.c                   # Main application entry point
│   ├── system_stm32f4xx.c       # System initialization code
│   └── util.c                   # Utility implementations
└── README.md                   # Project documentation
